test_command=for t in tests/*_test.sh; do sh "$t" || exit 1; done
id=roles-01 result=green reason=test_roles_01 (tests/roles_test.sh, new: pins coder.prompt's Input Rule ownership bullet stated by write surface — reads spdd/changes/ and spdd/specs/ as read-only context, spdd/specs/ never written, writes the code and tests the sub-spec calls for wherever they belong in the project plus the receipt in spdd/changes/<slug>/, never touches spdd/archive/ — refuses the old "Read only from" wording everywhere in the prompt, keeps the missing-dir/missing-sub-spec/OPEN_QUESTIONS/multi-layer stops verbatim, and guards the five-bullet count)
id=roles-02 result=green reason=test_roles_02 (tests/roles_test.sh, new: the ## Owns line, the rewritten bullet, and the ## Receipt section name the same surfaces; the Receipt section still carries 02-receipts' sentinel grammar verbatim, so the receipt duty is unchanged by this sub-spec)
id=roles-03 result=green reason=test_roles_03 (tests/roles_test.sh, new: the verifier Merge & Archive move is a plain mv as the only mechanism with the reason stated in the prompt — git mv on untracked files always fails, nothing here is ever committed — the release-gate half survives, git mv appears exactly once and only as that failure reason with the offered-alternative shapes refused, and the ADD/MODIFY/REMOVE merge and never-archive-a-rejected-change rules stand)
id=roles-04 result=green reason=test_roles_04 (tests/roles_test.sh, new: the Strict directory ownership gotcha bullet is exactly one line per doc, byte-identical between AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md, states the write-surface contract including the verifier merge half, and both docs refuse the old only-reads-changes and never-touch-specs claims anywhere)
id=roles-05 result=green reason=test_roles_05 (tests/roles_test.sh, new: tests/skills-activation-prompts_test.sh passes after the rewrites with both additive-vs-HEAD guards retired by loud printed note — test_additive_only_verifier gated through verifier_prompt_distinct_from_head mirroring 02's test_coder_additive_only gate, guard functions kept not deleted — no test outside roles_test.sh references the removed wording, and the receipts and closingblock suites run green with no edits)
